# Paths where a change always needs the owner's own review, even under the
# standing autonomous-operation grant that otherwise lets an ordinary,
# gate-passing change merge without a separate review step. Everything not
# listed here merges once the quality gate passes; nothing listed here does,
# regardless of how small the change looks.
#
# This file is the single source of that enforcement. The test under
# tests/Architecture walks the real tree for files belonging to a sensitive
# zone and fails when one of them is not matched here — so a new policy, a
# new admin surface over money, or a new migration touching the credential
# tables cannot arrive unowned and unnoticed. Patterns are written as globs
# rather than as one line per file for the same reason: the next file in a
# zone should be covered on the day it is written, not on the day someone
# remembers this file exists.

# Authentication and second-factor handling. Authenticate* is listed though
# the framework owns that middleware today — a published copy must land
# owned, not slip in as an ordinary change.
/app/Http/Middleware/Authenticate* @teratron
/app/Http/Middleware/EnsureSecondFactor* @teratron
/config/auth.php @teratron

# Authorization itself — policies, the scoping services behind them, and the
# permission/role registry a policy's decision ultimately reads. Token tables
# belong here too: how long a credential lives is an authorization question.
/app/Policies/ @teratron
/app/Services/Authorization/ @teratron
/config/permission.php @teratron
/database/seeders/*Permission* @teratron
/database/seeders/*Role* @teratron
/database/migrations/*permission* @teratron
/database/migrations/*role* @teratron
/database/migrations/*personal_access_token* @teratron

# Money — the financial ledger, the placement/commerce services that write to
# it, and every admin surface built over either, wherever it is nested.
/app/Models/FinancialRecord* @teratron
/app/Services/Placement/ @teratron
/app/Filament/**/FinancialRecord* @teratron
/app/Filament/**/Placement* @teratron

# Secrets and credential wiring.
/.env.example @teratron
/.env.production.example @teratron
/config/services.php @teratron
/.github/workflows/ @teratron

# The gate's own two halves. A boundary that can rewrite or silence itself
# under the grant it enforces is not a boundary.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @teratron
/tests/Architecture/SensitiveZoneCodeownersTest.php @teratron
